            <ArticleTitle>A case of painful progressive peripheral neuropathy after successful pancreas transplantation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>249-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 30-year-old female with diabetes type 1 of 26 years underwent simultaneous pancreas and kidney transplantation. In spite of good function of both organs she developed a pseudotabetic polyneuropathy of a diabetic type.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
